def UNIFORMITY(eyebrow, back):   # "Unity, or uniformity?": Chapter 5's second question; Chapter 6's side path off the recap
    out = []; U = out.append
    U('<section class="slide room"><div class=eyebrow>%s</div>' % eyebrow + '<h2 style="max-width:none;font-size:clamp(48px,11vmin,136px)">Unity, or uniformity?</h2>'
      '<aside class=notes>Their answer: unity now, uniformity in God&rsquo;s time, and by steps. Thomas in 1809, Alexander in 1828 and 1839, Stone in 1832 and 1835.</aside></section>')
    U(BIGQ(Q('&ldquo;&hellip;nor, indeed, is there anything either in Scripture or the nature of things that should induce us to expect <b>an entire unity of sentiment in the present imperfect state</b>.&rdquo;', DA, 'Not yet'), 'clamp(34px,7.4vmin,92px)', '30ch') +
      N('From the Address. Unity of sentiment: everyone thinking alike. Thomas does not expect it this side of the kingdom.'))
    U(BIGQ(Q('&ldquo;&hellip;for no man can relinquish his opinions or practices till once convinced that they are wrong; and <b>this he may not be immediately</b>, even supposing they were so. One thing, however, he may do: when not bound by an express command, <b>he need not impose them upon others</b>&hellip;&rdquo;', DA + ', the Appendix', 'Hold it; do not impose it'), 'clamp(30px,6.2vmin,78px)', '38ch') +
      N('The principle, stated outright. Union does not wait for agreement: a brother keeps his opinion until he is convinced, and that may take time. What he gives up now is imposing it. It goes on: then &ldquo;the things, to them, are as good as dead, yea, as good as buried.&rdquo;'))
    U(BIGQ(Q('&ldquo;&hellip;we charitably hope that, <b>in due time, God will reveal even this unto them</b>; only let such neither refuse to come to the light, nor yet, through prejudice, reject it when it shines upon them.&rdquo;', DA, 'In due time'), 'clamp(32px,6.8vmin,86px)', '34ch') +
      N('Of &ldquo;dear brethren&rdquo; who are &ldquo;otherwise minded.&rdquo; An echo of Philippians 3:15: &ldquo;if in any thing ye be otherwise minded, God shall reveal even this unto you.&rdquo; What they owe is openness, not instant assent.'))
    U(BIGQ(Q('&ldquo;The Church may, and we believe will, come to such a Scriptural unity of faith and practice, that there will be <b>no schism in the body</b>&hellip;&rdquo;', DA, 'But it will come'), 'clamp(34px,7.4vmin,92px)', '30ch') +
      N('It goes on: &ldquo;no self-preferring sect of professed and acknowledged Christians rejecting and excluding their brethren. This can not be, however, till the offensive and excluding causes be removed.&rdquo; And: that all should have &ldquo;the same identical views of all Divinely revealed truths&hellip; appears to us morally impossible.&rdquo;'))
    U(BIGQ(Q('&ldquo;&hellip;a still higher and more perfect degree of uniformity is intended, though neither in the first nor second instance, <b>which are but so many steps toward it</b>&hellip;&rdquo;', DA + ', the Appendix', 'Step by step'), 'clamp(34px,7.4vmin,92px)', '30ch') +
      N('The steps: first, forbear with one another in love; second, stop pressing private opinions where Scripture is silent. Then, in time, &ldquo;the utter abolition of those minor differences,&rdquo; most of which, &ldquo;had they been let alone, would have been long since dead and gone.&rdquo;',
        'Proposition 6 says the same of inferences: they belong to &ldquo;the after and progressive edification of the Church.&rdquo;'))
    U(FND(BIGQ(Q('&ldquo;If you think your brother in error, labor in the spirit of love and meekness to convince him; but imposing zeal against him will only harden him&hellip; <b>A little longer forbearance with each others weakness, and truth will triumph.</b>&rdquo;', 'Barton W. Stone, &ldquo;An Address to the Churches of Christ,&rdquo; <i>Christian Messenger</i>, 1832', 'Stone, the year of the union'), 'clamp(32px,6.8vmin,86px)', '34ch')) +
      N('The same address as the &ldquo;polar star&rdquo; in the recap; this is the sentence that closes that paragraph. He wrote it to the newly united Christians and Reformers, already quarrelling over baptism for remission and weekly communion.'))
    U(FND(BIGQ(Q('&ldquo;It is urged by many churches that one part of worship every Lord&rsquo;s day, is to break bread, others are not so well convinced of this as being a duty. <b>It is humbly hoped that mutual forbearance will be exercised</b>, one towards the other on this practice, <b>till we all come into the unity of the faith</b>.&rdquo;', 'Barton W. Stone, <i>Christian Messenger</i>, 1832', 'Even on the Supper every Lord&rsquo;s day'), 'clamp(30px,6.2vmin,78px)', '38ch')) +
      N('p. 280. Just before: &ldquo;When they shall become more established, and better acquainted with their duty&hellip; then they will profitably meet together every Lord&rsquo;s day.&rdquo; Weekly communion, the practice we now take for granted, given time to grow. &ldquo;Till we all come into the unity of the faith&rdquo; is Ephesians 4:13.'))
    U(FND(BIGQ(Q('&ldquo;&hellip;we will not denounce you as either traitors or rebels against him that is crowned Lord of all, <b>because you cannot walk as fast as we</b>&hellip;&rdquo;', AC + ', <i>Christian Baptist</i>, 1828', 'Alexander, to the slower churches'), 'clamp(34px,7.4vmin,92px)', '30ch')) +
      N('&ldquo;An Appeal to the Uncharitable,&rdquo; <i>Christian Baptist</i> 6 (September 1, 1828), p. 46. Reformers inside Baptist churches, threatened with non-fellowship by churches that would not move. Here the reformers are the faster ones, asking not to be cut off.',
        'Just before: &ldquo;we will bear with your mistakes and your misunderstandings, so long as they appear not to proceed from a perverse obliquity of will, but from a simple misapprehension of the will of our Lawgiver.&rdquo;'))
    U(FND(BIGQ(Q('&ldquo;So far as we are agreed in our apprehensions and sentiments, <b>&lsquo;let us walk by the same rule, let us mind the same thing;&rsquo;</b>&hellip; <b>We will commune with you</b> and welcome you to commune with us in all acts of religious worship&hellip;&rdquo;', AC + ', <i>Christian Baptist</i>, 1828', 'Walk by what we share'), 'clamp(30px,6.4vmin,80px)', '34ch')) +
      N('p. 47. Philippians 3:16: &ldquo;Nevertheless, whereto we have already attained, let us walk by the same rule, let us mind the same thing.&rdquo; The verse before is the Address&rsquo;s &ldquo;God shall reveal even this unto them&rdquo; (Philippians 3:15).',
        'The cut: &ldquo;and thus we will maintain unity and peace with all them of a pure heart.&rdquo; After: &ldquo;so long as you hold the head, and build upon the foundation of the Apostles and Prophets.&rdquo; Communion first, on what is shared.'))
    U(FND(BIGQ(Q('&ldquo;&hellip;by our mutual prayers and endeavors, <b>we shall come to be one in all the items of christian worship</b>, as we are now in the one body, the one spirit, the one hope, the one Lord, the one faith, the one immersion, the God and Father of all.&rdquo;', AC + ', <i>Christian Baptist</i>, 1828', 'One now; one in time'), 'clamp(30px,6.4vmin,80px)', '34ch')) +
      N('p. 47. Ephesians 4:4&ndash;6: one already (&ldquo;as we are now&rdquo;), one in worship still to come. Stone&rsquo;s &ldquo;till we all come into the unity of the faith&rdquo; is the same chapter, verse 13.',
        'Honest context: the same essay calls the &ldquo;most zealous opposers of reform&rdquo; &ldquo;carnal, worldly, speculative, and prayerless.&rdquo; Patient with the slow, hard on the hostile.'))
    U('<section class="slide breath"><h2 style="max-width:18ch;font-size:clamp(44px,9.6vmin,120px);line-height:1.15">They gave themselves the same time.</h2>'
      '<aside class=notes>Not only patience with others: each of them saw his own understanding as still growing.</aside></section>')
    U(FND(BIGQ(Q('&ldquo;&hellip;and therefore will not reject me for the lack of those fifty forms which might probably bring me up to your measure, and to which, if necessary, <b>I also, through grace, may yet attain, for I have not set myself down as perfect</b>.&rdquo;', 'Thomas Campbell, &ldquo;Protest and Appeal&rdquo; to the Associate Synod, 1808 or 1809', 'Thomas, to the synod that tried him'), 'clamp(32px,6.8vmin,86px)', '34ch')) +
      N('<i>Memoirs of Elder Thomas Campbell</i> (1861), pp. 12&ndash;15. Date disputed: Richardson and McAllister place it at the May 1808 appeal, but its &ldquo;my written declaration&rdquo; and &ldquo;once and again made application&rdquo; may fit his May 1809 paper to the Synod (research database, &ldquo;Thomas Campbell and the Seceders&rdquo;). Chapter 2&rsquo;s trial: he asks the Seceders to bear with him as he is ready to bear with them, &ldquo;where I can not see.&rdquo; The patience runs both ways.'))
    U(FND(BIGQ(Q('&ldquo;&hellip;yet a full emancipation from the traditions of the elders I had not experienced: <b>This was as gradual as the approaches of Spring</b>.&rdquo;', AC + ', <i>Christian Baptist</i>, 1830', 'Alexander, looking back'), 'clamp(36px,7.8vmin,98px)', '28ch')) +
      N('&ldquo;Concluding Remarks,&rdquo; pp. 307&ndash;308, closing the <i>Christian Baptist</i>. Just before: &ldquo;my own mind labored under the pernicious influence of scholastic divinity, and the Calvinian metaphysics.&rdquo; Twenty years from the token to here, and he calls it gradual.'))
    U(FND(BIGQ(Q('&ldquo;We worshipped separately for some time, till we became better acquainted&hellip; We began to worship together; this produced love; love destroyed our prejudices; and union was the result&hellip; <b>Neither side gave up any sentiment, or opinion, nor were they requested to do it.</b>&rdquo;', 'Barton W. Stone, <i>Christian Messenger</i>, 1835', 'The union, as Stone remembered it'), 'clamp(30px,6.2vmin,78px)', '38ch')) +
      N('Answer to J. V. Himes, pp. 43&ndash;44, on the 1832 union with the Reformers. Agreement was not the price of union; love came first, and the prejudices went after.'))
    U(FND(BIGQ(Q('&ldquo;I believe that that venerable correspondent will come out with a full declaration of faith&hellip; <b>But let him have his own time and his own manner</b> of communicating his conceptions.&rdquo;', AC + ', <i>Millennial Harbinger</i>, 1840', 'Alexander, of Stone'), 'clamp(32px,6.8vmin,86px)', '34ch')) +
      N('&ldquo;The venerable correspondent&rdquo; is Stone. A Baptist, Andrew Broaddus, faulted Stone&rsquo;s view of the atonement; Alexander would not. After their 1841 exchange: &ldquo;I can bear with a difference of opinion on a subject so vital, which many would regard as an insuperable obstacle to Christian communion.&rdquo;'))
    U(FND(BIGQ(Q('&ldquo;Let the Bible be substituted for all human creeds; facts, for definitions; things, for words; faith, for speculation; <b>unity of faith, for unity of opinion</b>&hellip; and the work is done.&rdquo;', CS.split(',')[0] + ', <i>The Christian System</i> (1839)', 'Alexander, 1839'), 'clamp(30px,6.4vmin,80px)', '34ch')) +
      N('&ldquo;Foundation of Christian Union,&rdquo; p. 115: &ldquo;the whole scheme of union&hellip; in one period.&rdquo; Unity of faith is the one Lord and the one confession, now. Unity of opinion is not required.'))
    U(BIGQ(Q('&ldquo;Duty then is ours; but <b>events belong to God</b>.&rdquo;', DA), 'clamp(44px,10vmin,124px)', '18ch') +
      N('From the Address, on whether the time is right for the attempt: &ldquo;whatever is to be done, must begin, some time, somewhere&hellip; if the Lord puts his hand to the work, it must surely prosper.&rdquo;'))
    U(CARD('Unity now.<br>' + G('Uniformity in God&rsquo;s time.'),
      'Unity is commanded and possible today: receive one another. Agreement on everything comes, if at all, by steps and in God&rsquo;s time, and is never a condition of fellowship.<br>' + back))
    return out

