# ---------- ALEXANDER AND THE SEA ----------
A('<section class="slide bleed" style="justify-content:center;padding:8vmin"><div class=bg><div class="bgimg wreckbg5"></div></div>'
  '<div class=credit>Philippe-Jacques de Loutherbourg, <i>A Shipwreck off a Rocky Coast</i> &middot; not the Hibernia</div>'
  '<div class=eyebrow style="font-size:clamp(20px,3.6vmin,44px);text-shadow:0 0 18px #000,0 0 6px #000">Islay, Scotland &middot; October 7, 1808</div>'
  '<h2 style="max-width:none;font-size:clamp(64px,14vmin,180px);line-height:1.05;text-shadow:0 0 30px #000,0 0 10px #000">Alexander and the Sea</h2>'
  '<aside class=notes>Chapter 2&rsquo;s last section, which we never reached. The son&rsquo;s story while the father&rsquo;s is still open: his father is in America, and has just broken with the Seceders (September 13, 1808), though no one at home knows it; Alexander, twenty, has been left in charge of the family. In Glasgow he will do, one after another, three things his father was charged with.</aside></section>')
